# Privacy notice — {{ rec.short }} community platform

**Information under Article 13 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) — version {{ doc.version }}**

This notice covers {{ rec.short }}'s digital platform:

- the online membership application;
- the community app, including its {% if features.ai_assistant %}AI assistant and its {% endif %}notifications;
- the login service.

{{ rec.short }}'s general privacy notice for members still applies to your membership
itself.{% if features.dso_data_exchange %} The separate notice "Sharing your meter readings" covers the optional sharing of
your meter readings.{% endif +%}

## 1. Who is responsible

The data controller is **{{ rec.name }}**.

- Address: {{ rec.registered_office }}, {{ rec.country.en }}.
- Tax code and VAT: {{ rec.tax_code }}.
- PEC: {{ rec.pec }}.
- Privacy contact: **{{ rec.privacy_contact }}**.
- Data protection officer: {{ rec.dpo }}.

{{ rec.short }} has entrusted the operation of the platform to **{{ platform.name }}**, {{ platform.registered_office }},
which processes your data on {{ rec.short }}'s behalf and on its instructions (Article 28
GDPR).

## 2. What data, and why

### 2.1 Your membership application

**What we collect:**

- your name and surname, tax code, email address and phone number;
- the address and POD code of your supply point;
- the information you give about your property and your energy equipment (solar panels,
  battery, electric vehicle, heat pump);
{% if features.document_extraction %}
- your choices on the consent page;
- if you choose to upload them, a copy of an electricity bill and of your identity
  document.
{% else %}
- your choices on the consent page.
{% endif %}

**What we do with it:**

{% if features.sms_verification %}
- We verify your phone number with a one-time code sent by SMS.
{% endif %}
{% if features.document_extraction %}
- If you upload a bill or an identity document, an artificial intelligence model reads
  it and fills in the form for you. From the bill it reads only your name, tax code,
  POD code, supply address and municipality. From the identity document it reads only
  your name, tax code and the document's expiry date. You check and correct what it
  read before you send the application. The model is an open-weight model on {{ platform.short }}'
  own server in {{ platform.city }}, {{ platform.country.en }}. The documents are **not** sent to any external AI
  provider and are **not** used to train AI models.
- The copies you upload are stored encrypted, so that {{ rec.short }}'s staff can check the
  application against them. They are deleted from the platform when your account is
  activated. What remains is the record that {{ rec.short }} checked your identity, and
  how.
{% endif %}
{% if features.existing_members %}
- {% filter wordwrap(85) | indent(2) %}
If you declare that you are already a member of {{ rec.short }}, the application may skip some of its steps for you. {{ rec.short }}'s staff then complete your POD code, and where needed your supply address, from the community's member register: the data you gave {{ rec.short }} when you joined. If they do not find you in the register, the application is rejected and you are invited to apply as a new member.
{%- endfilter +%}
{% endif %}
- We check your supply address against the areas of the community's configurations.
  This decides which configuration you belong to.
- Staff of {{ rec.short }} review the application. A person decides on admission.
- {% filter wordwrap(85) | indent(2) %}
If information you gave turns out to be wrong (for example, your POD code), {{ rec.short }} corrects it. It keeps a record of the previous value and of who made the correction.
{%- endfilter +%}

**Basis:**

- the steps you ask for before joining (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR);
- the legal requirements for renewable energy communities, Legislative Decree 199/2021
  (Article 6(1)(c)).

**Automatic area check:** if the check finds your address outside the community's
areas, the application cannot continue. You can write to the privacy contact to have
the check reviewed by a person.
{% if features.existing_members %}

Where staff complete your supply address from the member register, there is no automatic
refusal: the register's address decides the area.
{% endif %}

### 2.2 Your account

**What we keep:**

- your username, email address, name and preferred language;
- the record of your logins.

**Why:** to give you secure access to the platform.

**Basis:**

- the platform's terms of use (Article 6(1)(b));
- for the login record, {{ rec.short }}'s legitimate interest in keeping the platform secure
  (Article 6(1)(f)).

### 2.3 The community app

**What we use:**

- the energy data of the meters and devices registered to you in the community;
- forecasts and estimates derived from that data;
- your responses to suggestions, your commitments and your points;
- your app settings.

**Why:**

- to show you your consumption and production;
- to show you forecasts, suggestions for shifting consumption, points and badges.

**Basis:** your membership and the community rules (Article 6(1)(b)).

**How suggestions and points are produced:** they are worked out automatically from
your energy data.

- They are suggestions only.
- They have no legal effect on you.
- They do not change what {{ rec.short }} pays you.

**Leaderboards** show only your position, never your name.

### 2.4 Notifications

**What we use:**

- your notification preferences;
- your email address;
- the technical address your browser gives us when you allow push notifications;
- a record of which notifications were delivered, read and opened.

**Why:** to send you notifications about your energy and the community. Notifications
are selected by rules on your energy data, at most a few per day.

**Your control:**

- You can turn each kind of notification off in the app's settings.
- Weather alerts cannot be turned off.

**Basis:** the terms of use (Article 6(1)(b)).

{% set skip = 0 if features.ai_assistant else 1 %}
{% if features.ai_assistant %}
### 2.5 The AI assistant

**What we use:**

- the messages you write;
- the files you attach;
- the answers produced;
- the information the assistant reads for you to answer, with your own permissions:
  your energy data, your membership, your commitments, and the weather.

**What the assistant is:** an artificial intelligence system. Its answers can be wrong.

**Where it runs:**

- an open-weight language model on {{ platform.short }}' own server in {{ platform.city }}, {{ platform.country.en }};
- your conversations are kept on the platform.

**What happens to your conversations:**

- They are **not** sent to any external AI provider.
- They are **not** used to train AI models.

**Basis:** the terms of use, for a feature you choose to use (Article 6(1)(b)).

**Please do not** attach identity documents or other people's personal data.

{% endif %}
### 2.{{ 6 - skip }} Feedback

**What we use:** when you send feedback, your rating and comment, together with
technical details:

- the page;
- your browser and screen size;
- your IP address;
- **a screenshot of the page you were on**.

**Basis:** {{ rec.short }}'s legitimate interest in improving the platform (Article 6(1)(f)).

Sending feedback is voluntary. Check what is on screen before you send it.

### 2.{{ 7 - skip }} Records of what you accepted and chose

**What we keep:**

- which version of each document you accepted or read, and when;
- the IP address you did it from;
- each consent you gave or withdrew, with the text you were shown.

**Basis:** {{ rec.short }}'s obligation to be able to demonstrate them (Articles 5(2) and
7(1) GDPR; Article 6(1)(c)).

### 2.{{ 8 - skip }} Updates from {{ rec.short }}

If you asked to be kept updated, we use your email address to send you news about the
community.

**Basis:** your consent (Article 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw it at any time, through the
link in each message or by writing to the privacy contact.

## 3. Is providing the data required?

The data in §2.1 and §2.2 is needed to apply for membership and to use the platform.
